  "question": {
    "text": "A gas mixture consists of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of oxygen and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;moles of argon at temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>. Assuming the gases to be ideal and the oxygen bond to be rigid, the total internal energy (in units of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math>) of the mixutre is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>",
